      "verdict": "measured",
      "summary": "Trained in this repository by scenario `skin_cancer_isic`, loaded from the local checkpoint `skin_cancer_isic.pt`. Its 2 training manifests are on disk, so every one of the 1,003 test images can be checked against what the model saw.",
      "details": {
        "explain": {
          "what": "Every other number in this report assumes the model never saw these images. Whether that can be checked depends on where the model came from: a model trained here comes with the list of images it trained on, so the overlap can be counted. A model downloaded from someone else usually comes with no such list, and then the overlap cannot be counted at all.",
          "how": "Read the source first — trained here, or downloaded — and then whether a training record was found. With a record, the split check above is the real answer. Without one, the corpus check beside it is the only leakage check left, and it can only say whether leakage is possible, never that it did not happen.",
          "limits": "A training record says what its author declared. It cannot prove that nothing else was used — a model fine-tuned from another checkpoint inherits whatever that checkpoint saw, and no record here would show it."
        },
        "better": {},
        "baseline": {
          "kind": "ideal",
          "value": true,
          "basis": "a declared training record the split can be checked against",
          "cleared": true,
          "claim": "The model's training data is on record, so the split could be checked image by image.",
          "gap": null
        }
      },
      "plots": [],
